IMPORT prelude

-- Limitation Act 1974 (Tas), child abuse claims -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the
-- daydate library. The periods this encoding needs run "3 years [or 6] commencing on the date of discoverability" (s 5A(3),
-- (5)) and are suspended day by day (s 26A(3)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the child abuse claims encoding`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `falls before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `until` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the eve of` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` MINUS 1)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the sooner of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `falls before` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of month` m `in` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day and month n years later; 29 February falls on 28 February in a year that has none (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day` n `years on from` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the length of month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `in` `the year reached`)) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `the year reached`
    WHERE
        `the year reached` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS n

-- The 18th birthday (fork F4): the same day 18 years on; for a birth on 29 February, 28 February.
GIVEN `the birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 18th birthday for birth on` `the birth day` MEANS `the same day` 18 `years on from` `the birth day`

-- The last day of a period of n years "commencing on" a day (s 5A(3), (5)): the day itself is the first day, so the
-- period ends the day before the same day n years on; from 29 February into a year without one, it ends on 28 February,
-- the last day before 1 March (fork F1).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the first day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the final day of` n `years commencing on` `the first day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the first day` GREATER THAN `the length of month` (DATE_MONTH `the first day`) `in` (DATE_YEAR `the first day` PLUS n)
    THEN `the same day` n `years on from` `the first day`
    ELSE `the eve of` (`the same day` n `years on from` `the first day`)
